  <h1>What Is IVD?</h1>
  <p><strong>Direct answer:</strong> IVD (in vitro diagnostics) is the testing of samples — blood, serum, plasma, urine, swab or stool — outside the human body to detect diseases, conditions or infections. "In vitro" means "in glass", i.e. outside the body.</p>

  <h2>What it covers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Rapid tests / POCT</strong> — lateral-flow and fluorescence tests giving results in minutes at the point of care.</li>
    <li><strong>Laboratory immunoassays</strong> — ELISA, chemiluminescence for batch and quantitative testing.</li>
    <li><strong>Molecular diagnostics</strong> — PCR and nucleic-acid amplification.</li>
    <li><strong>Clinical chemistry &amp; urinalysis</strong> — reagent strips and analyzers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it matters</h2>
  <p>IVD underpins the majority of clinical decisions — screening, diagnosis, monitoring and treatment guidance — without needing to sample tissue from inside the body. For B2B buyers, IVD is the category that covers rapid tests, reagents and instruments.</p>

